      },
      "configs": {
        "recipe": {
          "model_roles": {
            "extraction": null,
            "small": null,
            "embedder": "chromadb DefaultEmbeddingFunction: all-MiniLM-L6-v2 ONNX (chroma-onnx-models onnx.tar.gz, sha256 913d7300ceae3b2dbc2c50d1de4baacab4be7b9380491c27fab7418616a16ec3), baked into the image",
            "dims": 384,
            "reranker": null
          },
          "notes": "The vendor's no-LLM benchmark modes. Both benchmark scripts build each palace with chromadb directly (`client.create_collection('mempal_drawers')`, no embedding_function, so ChromaDB's default all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and its default l2 space), the same model mempalace's own `minilm` default wraps (embedding.py; the image build checks the two give the same vector). `raw` is the vendor's default `--mode raw`; `hybrid` is locomo_bench.py `--mode hybrid` without `--llm-rerank`. No LLM is called on ingest or retrieval, so this config makes zero provider calls."
        },
        "common": {
          "supported": false,
          "model_roles": {
            "extraction": null,
            "embedder": null,
            "dims": null
          },
          "unsettable": [
            "extraction",
            "embedder"
          ],
          "notes": "Not built. The system has no extraction model, and this bundle runs only the local-embedder benchmark modes; the shim refuses SHIM_CONFIG=common at start. mempalace 3.10.0 can send embeddings to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (embedding_model openai-compat), which a later common arm could route through the proxy."
        }
      },
      "time": "native",
      "time_notes": "event_time is stored as the drawer's `timestamp` metadata, where the vendor benchmark stores the session date, and returned as each item's valid_from. The drawer text carries no date (the vendor's session document has none), and neither recipe reads a reference date, so query_time is ignored.",
      "provenance": {
        "status": "exact",
        "mechanism": "one drawer per session whose ChromaDB id is the session's source_id; every item is one whole drawer, so it cites exactly that session"
      },
      "delete": "native",
      "delete_notes": "ChromaDB `collection.delete(ids=[source_id])` on the session's drawer, then `collection.get(ids=[source_id])` confirms it is gone. Nothing is derived across drawers, so no residue is expected.",
      "readiness": "synchronous: ChromaDB embeds and indexes each drawer inside `upsert`, so /ingest returns after the write is searchable and /finish only reports the drawer count",
      "namespace": "palace: one ChromaDB PersistentClient per namespace at /data/palaces/<ns>/palace, collection mempal_drawers",
      "parallel_namespaces": false,
      "retrieval_policies": {
        "vendor-default": {
          "settings": {
            "recipe": "raw",
            "k": 10
          },
          "maps_to": "collection.query(query_texts=[question], n_results=10): locomo_bench.py's default --mode raw and --top-k 10 (session granularity). `--policy-setting recipe=hybrid` runs the vendor's hybrid recipe at the same k: query 3k candidates, then fused = distance * (1 - 0.50 * predicate-keyword overlap) * (1 - 0.60 * quoted-phrase hits) * (1 - 0.20 * person-name hits), keep the top k"
        },
        "fixed-evidence": {
          "settings": {
            "recipe": "raw",
            "k": 50
          },
          "maps_to": "the same call with n_results=50 (the vendor's documented --top-k 50 run and longmemeval_bench.py's 50-candidate pool), so the harness packer, not the vendor cutoff, decides what fits the evidence budget; recipe=hybrid queries 150 candidates and keeps 50"
        }
      },
      "recipes": {
        "raw": "vector search only: the vendor's headline no-LLM mode",
        "hybrid": "locomo_bench.py --mode hybrid with the LLM reranker off: vector candidates re-ranked by keyword, quoted-phrase and person-name boosts"
      },
      "streaming": "disabled",
      "telemetry_off": [
        "ANONYMIZED_TELEMETRY=False",
        "HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1",
        "HF_HUB_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1"
      ],
      "agent_surface": {
        "kind": "none",
        "transport": null,
        "version": "mempalace 3.10.0 ships an MCP server (mempalace-mcp); it is not wired here, because the shim builds palaces with the benchmark's ChromaDB calls rather than the mempalace miner"
      },
      "deviations_from_vendor_code": [
        "Sessions arrive one at a time through /ingest and are upserted into a persistent palace per namespace; the vendor builds one palace per conversation from all sessions in one add call and deletes it afterwards. Both insert in session order; HNSW search is approximate, so batching could change near-ties at the margin.",
        "Drawer ids are the opaque source ids (src-...) instead of doc_<i>, and the corpus_id metadata is the source id instead of session_<n>, so no dataset identity crosses the sanitizer.",
        "The timestamp metadata is the ISO event_time; the vendor copies LoCoMo's raw date string. Neither recipe reads it.",
        "Every dataset uses the LoCoMo session document (every turn as `Speaker said, \"text\"`). longmemeval_bench.py indexes user turns only, joined by newlines; the shim cannot tell datasets apart, so it keeps all turns, which also lets questions about what the assistant said find their session.",
        "The hybrid recipe is locomo_bench.py's (predicate keywords 0.50, quoted phrases 0.60, person names 0.20 over 3k candidates). longmemeval_bench.py's hybrid modes (v1 to v4: keyword weight 0.30, question-date boosts, assistant-reference two-pass, synthetic preference drawers, and v4's three fixes tuned on named LongMemEval misses) are not run, because they depend on LongMemEval's question_date format and question wording.",
        "The scoring loop in run_benchmark is re-implemented in shim.py with the vendor's constants; the corpus builder, keyword, quoted-phrase and person-name helpers and the query call are the vendor's own functions, imported from the pinned locomo_bench.py.",
        "The embedder is baked into the image at build time and the container runs with no route to the internet; the vendor downloads it on first use."
      ]
    }
  },
